      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Procedural order",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_001",
      "turn_index": 0,
      "speaker_id": "spk_001",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_002",
      "unit_text": "The House will now proceed to the debate on the regulation of artificial intelligence and workforce automation.",
      "char_start": 7,
      "char_end": 118,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Topic introduction",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_001",
      "turn_index": 0,
      "speaker_id": "spk_001",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_003",
      "unit_text": "I call Dr. Sarah Wollaston to move the motion.",
      "char_start": 119,
      "char_end": 165,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Procedural floor handoff",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_004",
      "unit_text": "Thank you, Mr. Speaker.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 23,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Politeness marker",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_005",
      "unit_text": "The government must establish an independent statutory authority to regulate autonomous workplace artificial intelligence before widespread deployment causes irreversible economic disruption.",
      "char_start": 24,
      "char_end": 215,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Central motion: statutory authority required",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_006",
      "unit_text": "According to the 2023 report from the Office for National Statistics, approximately 1.5 million jobs across the United Kingdom are at high risk of full automation within the next decade.",
      "char_start": 216,
      "char_end": 402,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "ONS 2023 report figures",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_007",
      "unit_text": "If we fail to establish enforceable standards today, displaced workers will bear the concentrated cost while corporate platforms privatize the productivity gains.",
      "char_start": 403,
      "char_end": 565,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Sub-claim regarding concentrated economic costs",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_008",
      "unit_text": "Will the honorable lady give way?",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 33,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Intervention request",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_004",
      "turn_index": 3,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_009",
      "unit_text": "I gladly give way to the right honorable gentleman.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 51,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Intervention grant",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_010",
      "unit_text": "I am grateful to the honorable lady",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 35,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Courtesy preamble",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_011",
      "unit_text": "her central premise is fundamentally flawed.",
      "char_start": 41,
      "char_end": 85,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "note": "Rhetorical objection preface",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_012",
      "unit_text": "History demonstrates that every major wave of technological innovation, from steam power to computerized banking, has created substantially more employment opportunities than it rendered obsolete.",
      "char_start": 86,
      "char_end": 282,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Historical precedent cited as empirical evidence",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_013",
      "unit_text": "Imposing rigid statutory constraints at this early juncture will stifle British technological innovation and drive frontier tech investment abroad to less restrictive jurisdictions.",
      "char_start": 283,
      "char_end": 464,
      "component_label": "COUNTERARGUMENT",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Objection that regulation harms UK investment",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_006",
      "turn_index": 5,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_014",
      "unit_text": "I thank the right honorable gentleman",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 37,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Courtesy",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_006",
      "turn_index": 5,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_015",
      "unit_text": "his historical analogy is dangerously inadequate for cognitive automation.",
      "char_start": 43,
      "char_end": 117,
      "component_label": "REBUTTAL",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Direct rebuttal targeting Clark's analogy",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_006",
      "turn_index": 5,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_016",
      "unit_text": "Unlike previous mechanical revolutions that replaced physical labor while creating cognitive clerical roles, generative algorithms directly substitute for cognitive analysis and administrative tasks simultaneously.",
      "char_start": 118,
      "char_end": 332,
      "component_label": "REBUTTAL",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Continuing rebuttal on generative automation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_006",
      "turn_index": 5,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_017",
      "unit_text": "A study published last month by Oxford University found that modern machine learning models compress clerical wage growth by 4.2 percent in early-adopter sectors without creating corresponding entry-level employment.",
      "char_start": 333,
      "char_end": 549,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Oxford University study findings",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_006",
      "turn_index": 5,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_018",
      "unit_text": "We cannot rely on nineteenth-century economic optimism to solve twenty-first-century algorithmic displacement.",
      "char_start": 550,
      "char_end": 660,
      "component_label": "REBUTTAL",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Concluding refutation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_007",
      "turn_index": 6,
      "speaker_id": "spk_004",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_019",
      "unit_text": "The government agrees that workforce safety is paramount",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 56,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "note": "Government stance anchor on safety",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_007",
      "turn_index": 6,
      "speaker_id": "spk_004",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_020",
      "unit_text": "our pro-innovation regulatory framework already equips existing sector regulators to address automated risk without creating costly new bureaucracy.",
      "char_start": 62,
      "char_end": 210,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Government policy thesis on sectoral regulation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_007",
      "turn_index": 6,
      "speaker_id": "spk_004",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_021",
      "unit_text": "Over the past twelve months, the Department for Science, Innovation and Technology has allocated 100 million pounds to targeted technical upskilling partnerships across twenty-four further education colleges.",
      "char_start": 211,
      "char_end": 419,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "100m pound budget allocation evidence",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_001_hansard",
      "source_corpus": "uk_hansard",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_007",
      "turn_index": 6,
      "speaker_id": "spk_004",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_022",
      "unit_text": "A rigid, centralized statutory ban would paralyze innovation, whereas agile sectoral oversight balances public accountability with continuous technological leadership.",
      "char_start": 420,
      "char_end": 587,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Supporting rationale for sectoral oversight",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    }
